    <h1>About Yoga Shakti</h1>
    <p>Yoga Shakti is a space to come back to yourself — through breath, stillness, and the practical wisdom of the classical texts. The teaching is grounded and unhurried: yoga for stress, sleep, focus, and calm, for beginners and seasoned practitioners alike.</p>

    <h2>The path</h2>
    <p>Rooted in Tantra and the Guru–Shishya tradition, the practice draws on Hatha Yoga and the breath sciences — Nadi Shodhana, pranayama, and meditation — taught the way they were meant to be learned: slowly, safely, and authentically.</p>

    <h2>The lineage</h2>
    <p>Ashish Anant teaches as a direct disciple of revered Tantra Masters — Ma Shakti Devpriya Anandnath ji and Acharya Agyaatadarshan Anandnath ji — carrying a living tradition into everyday practice.</p>

    <h2>About Ashish Anant</h2>
    <p>Ashish Anant is a yoga teacher in the Tantric tradition and a direct disciple of revered Tantra Masters Ma Shakti Devpriya Anandnath ji and Acharya Agyaatadarshan Anandnath ji. His teaching is warm, unhurried, and deeply practical — yogic wisdom made usable for everyday life. He holds complimentary live sessions and the Nadi Shodhana healing-breath workshop, welcoming beginners and seasoned practitioners alike.</p>

    <h2>Come practise</h2>
    <p>Join a complimentary live session, learn the healing breath in the Nadi Shodhana workshop, or begin with the simple Yogic Breathing Guide. Everything starts with one slow breath.</p>
